    "user_request_original": "Design a 23-layer planar multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate at normal incidence. Layer sequence: Air | Si | Al2O3 | Si | Al2O3 | Si | Al2O3 | Si | Al2O3 | Si | Al2O3 | Si | Al2O3 | Si | Al2O3 | Si | Al2O3 | Si | Al2O3 | Si | Al2O3 | Si | Al2O3 | Si | CaF2. Initialize inner 22 layers with thicknesses from iteration_15 best candidate [502, 538, 621, 599, 496, 583, 612, 497, 535, 545, 906, 627, 613, 510, 545, 606, 629, 1017, 461, 450, 576, 865] nm, initialize outer layer (layer 1) to 550 nm quarter-wave at 3.3 um. Thickness optimization bounds: 400-1265 nm for all layers. Optimize for high transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands, low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 2500-3100 nm, 3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm, 4450-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands; Low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 24; No metal layers; Conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials only.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Design and thickness-optimize a 23-layer planar Si/Al2O3 alternating stack on a CaF2 substrate at normal incidence. Initialize the first layer to 550 nm and the remaining 22 layers with the provided iteration_15 thickness values, constrained between 400 and 1265 nm. Maximize transmittance in the 3.25–3.35 µm and 4.20–4.30 µm bands while minimizing transmittance in the 2.50–3.10 µm and 4.45–5.00 µm bands across a 2.5–5.0 µm spectrum.",
